        "date": "Sun, 25 Oct 2026 17:17:46 GMT",
        "server": "uvicorn"
      },
      "body": "\"This email template is designed to be professional, reassuring, and clear. It ensures the customer knows exactly what happened without requiring them to search through complex system messages.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Professional Email Template\\n\\n**Subject:** ✅ Your Subscription Update Has Been Successfully Processed\\n\\n**Dear [Customer Name],**\\n\\nWe are pleased to confirm that your subscription update has been successfully processed.\\n\\nWe have successfully applied the changes to your account, and your new plan is now active.\\n\\n### **Subscription Summary**\\n\\nFor your convenience, here are the details of your updated subscription:\\n\\n*   **Account:** [Customer Account ID or Email Address]\\n*   **Previous Plan:** [Name of Old Plan, e.g., Basic Tier]\\n*   **New Plan:** [Name of New Plan, e.g., Premium Pro]\\n*   **Effective Date:** [Date the change took effect, e.g., Immediately / Start of next billing cycle on MM/DD/YYYY]\\n*   **Billing Cycle:** [Monthly / Annually]\\n*   **New Monthly/Annual Price:** [New Price, e.g., $49.99/month]\\n\\nYou can now enjoy all the benefits associated with the **[New Plan Name]**.\\n\\n### **What Happens Next?**\\n\\nYou should receive a separate confirmation email regarding your new billing cycle and any immediate changes to your service features within the next [X] hours.\\n\\nIf you have any questions about your new plan, features, or billing details, please do not hesitate to contact our support team.\\n\\n**[Link to Help Center/FAQ Page]**\\n\\nThank you for being a valued customer of [Your Company Name].\\n\\n**Best regards,**\\n\\n**[Your Name]**\\n[Your Title/Department, e.g., Customer Success Team]\\n[Your Company Name]\\n[Your Direct Support Phone Number (Optional)]\\n[Your Company Website Link]\\n\\n---\\n\\n### 💡 Quick Tips for Implementation:\\n\\n1.  **Personalization is Key:** Always use the customer's name (`[Customer Name]`).\\n2.  **Clarity over Jargon:** Avoid internal technical terms. Focus on what the *customer* gains (e.g., \\\"enjoy all the benefits\\\").\\n3.  **Specific Dates:** Providing the effective date helps prevent confusion about when the change actually started.\\n4.  **Test the Links:** Ensure the link to the FAQ or Help Center is working correctly.\\n5.  **Automation:** This email should ideally be triggered automatically by your billing system immediately after the successful update.\"",
